{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: prepare and deliver the focused I7 object-key probe decision amendment raised in #4220 and refreshed as #4223. I choose normal semantic key evaluation for selected extension calls, without the legacy preliminary whole-input probe for an extension-bearing key expression. This is an explicit, narrow compatibility amendment, not a claim that the old preliminary refusal behavior is preserved. The [current decision](notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md@756ce43a1db293cab3cbef522f3b9e380f6290c4:230) requires both preliminary checks and no speculative provider dispatch; [twelve independent controls](key-probe-controls.jsonl) reproduce the conflict and its mixed-key/empty-input boundaries. They use legacy callbacks, not admitted providers. Full runtime implementation remains on #4043.","body":{"branch":"request/i7-object-key-probe-decision","conditions":"In a new request/i7-object-key-probe-decision worktree from current main, amend only notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md concisely. This child owns the source decision amendment; independent compiler/physical/core work on4043 may continue while dependent dispatch waits for adoption and review.\n\nChosen rule: at compile/admission, classify each constructor key expression by a complete bounded walk of its admitted AST, including nested expressions and branches, for direct calls to selected extensions. Use resolved selected-call identity, not source-text matching or executing the expression. For such a key expression, omit the entire preliminary whole-input key evaluation; perform its ordinary per-item/tuple key evaluation exactly once at each existing semantic evaluation point, with the normal scope, key checks, provider call/work charging, failure ordering and all grouping completed before values. No dry-run provider, memoization, result reuse, alternate argument frame or uncharged speculative call. A key expression with no selected extension retains its existing preliminary check, evaluations and ordinary errors. Calls only in a group value do not change that group's key rule. Keep direct-call/no-reference/no-shadow/no-partial extension confinement.\n\nState the compatibility exception explicitly, including dormant selected-call branches: an extension-bearing mixed key whose whole-input pure branch returned a non-string may now yield valid per-item string keys instead of preliminary T1003. This also applies if the selected call sits in an untaken branch. Ordinary per-item invalid-key T1003, undefined keys, source key-expression order, duplicate-key D1009, lexical scopes and the adopted first-encounter group/value order stay. Preserve the existing empty/null/tuple discovery convention; when it creates a virtual undefined item, its one normal key evaluation is semantic and any executed selected call is charged once. Do not add a second whole-input provider probe or silently change empty input into a different invocation policy.\n\nRequire exact output/error/ordered-call/work/boundary fixtures: two identical explicit sites=two calls; false branch=zero; two-item path=two; two-item direct constructor key=two rather than three; whole-input-only provider branch=zero rather than one; grouped value=one; both mixed-key cases above; extension-free mixed-key control retains preliminary T1003; empty/null; invalid per-item key; nested key expression/group, tuple/reduce and two colliding key expressions. For the two-item {$count($)\u003e1 ? 7 : $probe(\"k\"):$} case, choose {\"k\":[1,2]} with two charged calls. For false?$probe(\"unused\"):($count($)\u003e1?7:\"k\") as the key, choose {\"k\":[1,2]} with zero calls. For {$count($)\u003e1?$probe(\"whole\"):7:$}, retain per-item T1003 with zero calls. Add omission/extra-dispatch and skipped-meter controls. Keep a paired extension-free corpus and all existing broader I7 gates; these examples are necessary cases, not a substitute for complete coverage.\n\nAccount for the changed evaluator/admission semantics in existing core.jsonata/grammar/dialect/corpus components wherever affected, keeping exactly ten identity components, old-identity recognition, stored-program revalidation before replay writes and unchanged projection/frontier on refusal. Preserve the separate acknowledged reset/activation boundary, all four delivery stages and eight gates. Do not add a component, automatic migration or production admission.\n\nPublish an exact amendment artifact with valid behavior provenance and clickable previews, and a concise ordinary adoption proposal for Hugh. I will ratify the exact proposal before independent Checker Architecture/Security/Simplification review. Ratify the independent verdict; seal only its approved exact head with path succession, push source/workroom refs, verify relevant CI, and remove owned worktree/branch. Any unresolved semantic counterexample must be raised before claiming the amendment complete. After adoption, implementation and eventual pin/callers stay on4043's existing promise. This child authorizes no public evaluator/module publication, live operation, reset or release.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:42c2ce37bf635f3fffa9b5109ec95ac513b92c49, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:4cb6181f8002285798b161b3adf8c10bcbad8ccb stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:01085058d588ea9651e2cf4037ac2d153c9461e3, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:4357cae21cccb883131fe9ad679696ad14ac14a5, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:658121585f7eb6d5c1b047c676e54867e5000c2b, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:8c17d9e03de8cacb255a59d1859dc84ef6f78c70","target_head":"756ce43a1db293cab3cbef522f3b9e380f6290c4","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}